09. S3 + Terraform:

This is extremely important for DevOps interviews.

Terraform state can be stored remotely in S3.

Instead of:

terraform.tfstate

sitting on your laptop:

Developer Laptop
     |
     v
terraform.tfstate

you can use remote state:

Terraform
    |
    v
S3
    |
    +-- terraform.tfstate

For team environments, this allows shared state storage.

Modern Terraform setups can also use a locking mechanism/configuration supported by the Terraform/AWS versions you're using; don't blindly assume older DynamoDB-locking examples are the only/current approach.


10. Why Remote Terraform State?

Suppose:

DevOps Engineer A
       |
       v
terraform.tfstate

and:

DevOps Engineer B
       |
       v
terraform.tfstate

You can get state-management problems.

With remote state:

Engineer A ──┐
              ├──> S3
Engineer B ──┘

Everyone works against the shared remote state.
